.TITLE "pbcopy"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Takes standard input and copies it to the macOS pasteboard (clipboard).
This command is useful for scripting and piping output from other commands
directly into the clipboard, making content available for pasting into
applications.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**copy**

.DIV "TLDR"
**pbcopy**
Copies the content of standard input to the clipboard.
> 

**echo "__text__" | pbcopy**
Copies a specific string of __text__ to the clipboard.
> __text__: The string to be copied.

**cat __file.txt__ | pbcopy**
Copies the content of a __file.txt__ to the clipboard.
> __file.txt__: The path to the file whose content will be copied.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`pbcopy` operates on standard input, so it is often used with pipes (`|`)
to capture the output of other commands. The clipboard content can then be
pasted using `pbpaste`.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:pbpaste**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/pbcopy.html
